@@ -96,6 +96,7 @@ The table above is the short list. This part covers the remaining `MOE_CACHE_*`
 | `MOE_CACHE_IDLE_REBALANCE_MS` | Idle refill: how many milliseconds without any graph running (an agent waiting for a tool) before the refill starts. 0 turns idle refill off. | 1500 | advanced |
 | `MOE_CACHE_LAN_ADDRS` | Tests only: a comma-separated list of addresses that `--lan` / `--ui-lan` use instead of asking the system for this PC's addresses (for example `192.168.1.20,203.0.113.5`). Do not set it for normal use. | unset (ask the system) | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_LAYERS` | Limits the cache to a range of layers, written `lo-hi` (for example `10-40`). Anything not in that form is ignored. | all layers | advanced |
+| `MOE_CACHE_LAYER_SHARE` | Plain LRU policy only: of the K oldest idle experts, evicts one from the layer holding the most cached experts, so one layer cannot hog the cache. K is clamped to 0 to 64; 0 turns it off. | 0 (off) | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_LINUX_VIEW_DROP` | Linux only. When the plugin lets go of a model-file mapping, `pageout` also drops those pages from the system file cache at once. Any other value keeps the default (pages stay cached but are first in line to be reclaimed). | Off (pages stay in the file cache, marked cold) | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_LINUX_VIEW_RANDOM` | Linux only. If set to anything (even empty), model-file mappings are tagged "random access" so the kernel reads ahead less. The code calls it an A/B test setting from the first prototype. | Off | internal/testing |
 | `MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD_CAP` | With lookahead prefetch on, the most experts per layer that are not yet in RAM and get read ahead. Numbers below 1 become 1. Ignored unless `MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD` is on. | 2 | advanced |
